  <h2>NotchOS</h2>
  <p>
    NotchOS turns the MacBook notch into a glass island for the tools you open all day: file tray, clipboard history,
    calendar, tasks, timers, teleprompter, system vitals, on-device writing tools, and Android Share. Closed, it can still
    show live activities (timer, music, downloads). One key unlocks one Mac. Start a 7-day trial in the app with no card.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/trial">Start free trial</a> · <a href="/download">Download</a> · <a href="/#features">Features</a></p>

  <h2>Notchy</h2>
  <p>
    Notchy is a polished native notch app with a large feature set and strong marketing content. It typically needs
    macOS 13+ and sells as a one-time license after a trial. See our
    <a href="/alternatives/notchy">Notchy alternatives</a> page and
    <a href="/compare/notchy-vs-notchos">Notchy vs NotchOS</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Alcove</h2>
  <p>
    Alcove focuses on a refined Dynamic Island feel — especially media. It often requires a newer macOS than the rest of
    the field. Details: <a href="/alternatives/alcove">Alcove alternatives</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>NotchNook</h2>
  <p>
    NotchNook (Lo.cafe) is known for its file tray and design language. Pricing is usually one-time or monthly. Details:
    <a href="/alternatives/notchnook">NotchNook alternatives</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Boring Notch</h2>
  <p>
    Boring Notch is free and open source — the default answer when someone searches for a free Dynamic Island for Mac.
    Scope is narrower than paid suites. Details: <a href="/alternatives/boring-notch">Boring Notch alternatives</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>DynamicLake</h2>
  <p>
    DynamicLake sits in the paid notch/widget space. Confirm current price and requirements on the vendor site. Details:
    <a href="/alternatives/dynamiclake">DynamicLake alternatives</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Atoll, Sapphire, Seam, Droppy, MediaMate</h2>
  <p>
    Newer or adjacent tools: <a href="/alternatives/atoll">Atoll</a> (free OSS),
    <a href="/alternatives/sapphire">Sapphire</a> (OSS + tiers, Android share),
    <a href="/alternatives/seam">Seam</a> (paid productivity / dictation),
    <a href="/alternatives/droppy">Droppy</a> (tray-focused), and
    <a href="/alternatives/mediamate">MediaMate</a> (HUD replacement, not a full island).
    Roundups: <a href="/blog/boring-notch-alternatives">Boring Notch alternatives</a>,
    <a href="/compare/alcove-vs-boring-notch">Alcove vs Boring Notch</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to choose</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Need free / open source:</strong> Boring Notch.</li>
    <li><strong>Need music polish above all:</strong> Alcove (check macOS version).</li>
    <li><strong>Need tray + design:</strong> NotchNook.</li>
    <li><strong>Need clipboard, prompter, Android Share, AI, timers in one island:</strong> NotchOS.</li>
  </ul>
